## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from B645)
8 cores. **Start a heavy run (`dotnet build`, `test`, `--list-tests`, `restore`, a mutant run, the full line) only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent; say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile. **Then take ONE slot atomically** (`mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '.../heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '.../heavy-slot-3'`), write `B663 <time> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first and never touch one; a slot directory with no holder is reported, never taken. One heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot; for a run longer than a few minutes also hold `.tools/b663/heavy.lock` (a directory, pid inside, released by a MOVE); at the end release ONLY your slot by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-25_B663_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b663/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a figure that does not move for 3 beats means stuck. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line: wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!` or a done-marker. SDK and homes SEAT-LOCAL: `<project root>/.tools/dotnet/dotnet` with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false`, `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`, `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1`; `DOTNET_CLI_HOME`, `NUGET_PACKAGES`, `NUGET_HTTP_CACHE_PATH`, `NUGET_PLUGINS_CACHE_PATH` under `.tools/b663/` set BEFORE the first restore and proven from each worktree's `obj/project.assets.json` `packageFolders`. Record `python3 --version`. Never leave a background job running; no artificial load.

## GRADING (binding; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **Blocker:** a path beyond the 4; any byte differing under the escalation paths; the head moved; a removed line beyond the 3 `src` lines and the one docs line; a real value from any book, a person's name, a secret in an added line, your STATUS or evidence; a skipped, failed or `Skip =` test; a warning, failed or skipped test in the whole line; a NEW open alert on the PR ref with security severity high or higher or rule severity `error`.
- **Major:** one of the four named walks lists more than 20 (or fewer than the first 20) at 100,000 lines, or a route bypasses the cap; the docs line not byte-equal to C-70; a string literal added in `src`; a reachable mutant of the cap surviving every committed row and the `QuoteApiTests` family (G-2; SAME CLASS = the walk-cap class); a case red for another reason than it names, green at base, or whose expectation is read from the code under test; a name lost or more than 10 added; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (10 cases, +137 -4, 2,847, kill counts); a failing check-run on the head or merge result; an analysis missing (4 of 4 required); a ticket key, finding id, mutant id, brief number or percent figure in the code lines, test names or commit message; non-ASCII in added lines; a build warning.
- **Minor:** an uncapped sibling walk not named by the ticket (ticket-shaped); a case depending on machine, culture, order or clock that cannot fail on Linux; a surviving equivalent proven so. **Note:** process disclosures, the PR body's brief number, the long docs line, style, CI state stated.
- **Verdict token.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green, 4 of 4 analyses with both thresholds met, the whole line green, R3 and R5 closed, 0 findings above Note. GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. NO GO = any Blocker or Major; list every Major+ by id and say if it is the walk-cap class (a second same-class NO GO is the cap: no round 3 without the product owner). A required check you could not run adds ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first AND last lines, never a bare GO; a check in progress at the verdict reads `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FINDINGS.

